      "text": "Reg 4.15(d) prescribes the use of a representation of the Arms or emblem of a city or town in Australia or of a public authority or public institution in Australia."
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Regs 4.15(da) and (e) prescribe the use of a representation of a “sign”, applicable to countries of the International Union for the Protection of Industrial Property as not entitled to registration under international arrangements. Article 6ter of the Paris Convention lists generally the kinds of signs which are to be refused registration.."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Article 6ter signs include the following:"
        },
        {
          "depth": 1,
          "kind": "list_item",
          "text": "Flags and coats of arms of Member States/countries"
        },
        {
          "depth": 1,
          "kind": "list_item",
          "text": "Emblems, badges etc of intergovernmental organisations"
        },
        {
          "depth": 1,
          "kind": "list_item",
          "text": "Badges of warranty and control, including hallmarks."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Under the terms of the Paris Convention, of which Australia became a member in 1907, a member state may refuse or cancel the registration of trade marks if they are the same as signs protected under Article 6ter."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "The provisions also apply where part of a trade mark is an Article 6ter sign and where a trade mark contains or consists of a sign so nearly resembling an Article 6ter sign that it is likely to be taken for it."
        }
      ],
      "cases": [],
      "chunk_ref": "TMM/Part31/2/2/5",
      "content_hash": "sha256:0fcab20c66cff950328e924b3773c70eb2acd1fbd350bd90f9ca1852edc1cf9a",
      "emphasis": [],
      "fragment": null,
      "heading_path": [
